## Bubble Sort

### 📌 Problem Description
Implement the Bubble Sort algorithm to sort an array of integers in ascending order by repeatedly comparing adjacent elements and swapping them if they are in the wrong order.

### 💡 Approach
1. Start from the first element of the array.
2. Compare each pair of adjacent elements.
3. Swap them if the current element is greater than the next element.
4. After each pass, the largest unsorted element moves to its correct position at the end of the array.
5. Repeat the process until the array is sorted or no swaps are needed.

### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis
- **Best Case:** O(n) — when the array is already sorted and an optimized implementation detects no swaps.
- **Average Case:** O(n²)
- **Worst Case:** O(n²)
- **Space Complexity:** O(1) — sorting is performed in place.

### 🛠️ Language
Java

###Solution

class Solution {
    public int[] bubbleSort(int[] nums) {
        for(int i=0;i<nums.length;i++)
        {
            boolean swapped=false;
            for(int j=0;j<nums.length-1-i;j++)
            {
                if(nums[j]>nums[j+1])
                {
                    int temp=nums[j];
                    nums[j]=nums[j+1];
                    nums[j+1]=temp;
                    swapped=true;
                }
            }
            if(!swapped) break;
        }
        return nums;
    }
}                                                                             
